{
  "_source": {
    "what": "ETSI TS 103 744 CatKDF known-answer test, parameter set HKDFwSHA384_P384_ML-KEM-768 (cid 2221, index 6 of the reference harness), copied VERBATIM from the C arrays of the reference implementation (hex, lowercased). Only this one parameter set is kept.",
    "spec": "ETSI TS 103 744 V1.2.2 (2026-02), clauses 7.2.3, 7.4.2, 8.2.3 and Annex C/D",
    "repository": "https://forge.etsi.org/rep/cyber/103744_QHKEX",
    "branch": "kats_v1.2.x",
    "commit": "135f6b71c564",
    "path": "main.c",
    "file_sha256": "2b34f6d2af60e424d36e9e9dfa6b4a283878802f67f32ea94bbcab845a23845a",
    "fields": "cid is the 2-byte ciphersuite id. labelA/labelB are the label contributions, label = labelA XOR labelB. pa1/pb1 are the ECDH public keys as the harness formats them in MA/MB: the raw x||y coordinates (96 bytes), WITHOUT the 0x04 prefix. pa2 is ML-KEM-768's encapsulation key, pb2 its ciphertext. k1 is the P-384 ECDH secret (the x coordinate), k2 the ML-KEM secret. MA = cid || len(labelA) || labelA || len(pa1) || pa1 || len(pa2) || pa2 and MB likewise with labelB/pb1/pb2 (Annex C m_format, 32-bit big-endian lengths). key_material = CatKDF(psk = empty, k1, k2, MA, MB, info, label, 24) with HKDF-SHA-384. ecdh_private_a is A's P-384 scalar and ecdh_public_b B's point in SEC1 uncompressed form; mlkem_keygen_seed (d||z) and mlkem_encaps_seed (m) are the derandomized ML-KEM inputs that produce pa2, pb2 and k2.",
    "public_test_data": "Every secret here is a published test value, not a credential."
  },
